{
  "schema_version": "capture-profiles-v1",
  "description": "Publisher capture profiles. Pure data: one registry drives the browser extension, the acquisition script and the intake sidecar mapping, so a selector never has to be fixed in three places. `status` is a measurement, not an intention -- `supported` requires a committed fixture that a test asserts against.",
  "status_meanings": {
    "supported": "A skeleton fixture is committed and a test asserts container, identity and the figure manifest against it.",
    "generic": "No publisher-specific selectors proven. Capture still works through the fallback selectors and records profile=generic.",
    "unsupported": "A measured blocker prevents capture. `reason` states what was observed.",
    "asset_origins": "Hosts other than the page's own origin that this publisher serves figures and stylesheets from. Nothing outside the page origin and this list is fetched, and nothing outside the page origin is fetched with the reader's cookies."
  },
